  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi></math>, let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>–</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>)</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>–</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>–</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></math> be one of its root. Then, among the two statements</p><p>(I) If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> cannot be the geometric mean of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math>.</p><p>(II) If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> may be the geometric mean of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math>.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
